55
00:01:50.030 --> 00:01:55.030 line:15%
A, does it mean "Put in Place" or B, "Mind Your Plate?"

56
00:01:56.590 --> 00:01:57.507
I know this one.

57
00:01:57.507 --> 00:01:58.640
(audience applauding and cheering)

58
00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:01.450
This is the first thing they taught me on the cooking show.

59
00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:02.640
I watched it.
Mise En Place.

60
00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:04.740
And it just means put all the stuff

61
00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:06.760
in little baskets or whatever,

62
00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:09.290
like in cups so that you can then, it's all done.

63
00:02:09.290 --> 00:02:10.630
And I actually think it's really good.

64
00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:12.480
You just measure out all your stuff

65
00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:14.780
and you put it in little cups.

66
00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:16.040
It does make more dishes,

67
00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:18.010
so the lazy side of me doesn't like that,

68
00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:20.180
but it's good especially if you're one of those people

69
00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:21.900
that looks at the recipe over and over again

70
00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:23.900
and Mise En Place.

71
00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:24.733
Let's see if you're right.

72
00:02:24.733 --> 00:02:26.640
The answer is A.

73
00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:29.630
Mise En Place means put in place.

74
00:02:29.630 --> 00:02:33.050
And what that refers to is do all of your prep work

75
00:02:33.050 --> 00:02:35.010
before you start cooking

76
00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:37.770
because it takes the stress out of cooking.

77
00:02:37.770 --> 00:02:39.380
Start there and I bet

78
00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:41.440
